{#- Credential strip. Added August 27, 2026.

    Renders the marks from _data/credentials.json under the hero on the three
    language homepages and the three All-Access pages. Content lives in the data
    file, never here — same reason library.json exists: the previous credential
    on this site was hand-written three times into one sales page, and the
    TrainingPeaks relationship appeared as a credential exactly once, inside a
    blurb an ATHLETE copy-pastes rather than anything Ivan says himself.

    `variant` (optional, set by the including page):
      "full"    — default. Label, five marks, the Coach Match line, About link.
      "compact" — marks only, no line, no link. For pages that already carry a
                  link to /sobre-ivan/ elsewhere and would otherwise repeat it.

    Deliberately NOT on every page. It sits where a stranger forms a first
    judgement (homepage) or is being asked for money (All-Access). The 328 plan
    pages get the one-line version from plan-page-content.njk instead — a full
    strip on a plan page competes with the buy button.                        -#}
{%- set cr = credentials[lang] -%}
{%- set variant = trustBarVariant or "full" -%}
<section class="trust-bar{% if variant == "compact" %} trust-bar-compact{% endif %}">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="label">{{ cr.barLabel }}</span>
    <ul class="trust-marks">
      {%- for item in cr.items %}
      <li class="trust-mark{% if item.badge %} has-badge{% endif %}">
        {%- if item.badge %}
        {#- width/height are set so the row never reflows while the image loads.
            `loading="lazy"` is deliberately NOT used: on the homepage this strip
            sits directly under the hero and is above the fold on desktop. -#}
        <img class="trust-badge" src="{{ item.badge | v }}" alt="{{ item.badgeAlt }}" width="40" height="40" decoding="async">
        {%- endif %}
        <span class="trust-mark-text">
          <span class="trust-mark-name">{{ item.name }}</span>
          <span class="trust-mark-note">{{ item.note }}</span>
        </span>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- if variant != "compact" %}
    <p class="trust-line">{{ cr.barLine }} <a href="{{ cr.aboutHref }}">{{ cr.aboutLabel }} →</a></p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>
